; EVERYTHING THAT IS READ RATHER THAN PRESSED.
;
; Inter is the theme's `default_font`: every Label, every card, every line of lore. It is
; the plainest thing here on purpose — body text has one job and character is not it.
;
; ⚠ WHY THIS EXISTS AT ALL, WHEN DejaVu WAS ALREADY THE DEFAULT. DejaVu was picked for
; COVERAGE (24/24 of the glyphs the font gate had to substitute) and it is still the one
; that provides it, underneath. But coverage and legibility are different jobs and it was
; doing both: DejaVu's letterforms are wide and dated next to a UI built in 2026. Inter
; on top, DejaVu behind, gets both — the reading face is clean and any symbol it lacks
; still draws.
;
; The pairing is the same shape as `display_font.tres`, for the same reason: a control
; resolves to ONE font and then falls through that FONT's own chain, never the theme's.
